{"game": "risk-of-rain-returns", "language": "english", "appid": 1337520, "month": "2026-05", "window": 4, "start_date": 1779580800, "end_date": 1780271999, "month_true_total": 72, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 00:55:38 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "226859370", "author": {"steamid": "76561198998652174", "personaname": "ツ OneMoreCawfee", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/daCawfeeSommelier/", "num_games_owned": 219, "num_reviews": 14, "playtime_forever": 218, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 35, "playtime_at_review": 182, "last_played": 1790399120, "avatar": "0c32f22b386a6af99b78e60126022b0411c2382b"}, "language": "english", "review": "Yoinked ROR1 when it came out, played it constantly back when I still had a Windows XP PC.\r\n\r\nProperly bought ROR2 a couple of years back, turned into a completionist with 100 something hours and still trying to 100% the game alongside Eclipses.\r\n\r\nBit the bullet and bought RORR a few weeks back, trying to find the old feeling of ROR1 while insisting that it would be a \"chilled ROR2\" since I would use a controller. Nope, it's just as chaotic, and hurts my wrist immensely because of how bad I held the controller but it's too good. I felt the feeling of the original ROR again.\r\n\r\nLove it. Still my first ever Rougelike series, the first series that managed to convince that I'm not just an FPS player, and one that I still play to this day. It better receives more update, Gearbox. <3", "timestamp_created": 1780229751, "timestamp_updated": 1780229751, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1699469751", "hardware": {"system_ram": "65325", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10500H CPU @ 2.50GHz", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA Ge